2. Free individual, non-commercial use

An individual acting solely in a personal capacity may use, copy, study, modify,
and share the Software without a license fee, solely for personal,
non-commercial purposes, subject to this license. Examples include personal
learning, experimentation, and personal projects that do not serve a commercial
purpose or an organization.

Non-commercial use means use that is not intended for or directed toward
commercial advantage, business operations, monetary compensation, or other
economic benefit, directly or indirectly. This permission does not cover work
for an employer, customer, client, business, enterprise, or other organization,
even when an individual performs that work or no fee is charged for the
Software itself, except as expressly permitted by section 3.

3. Free employer use

A "Qualifying Employer" is a legal entity that has employed, currently employs,
or later employs Jihad Khawaja. There is no employment-date cutoff based on
when this license or an earlier version was first made available. An entity
does not qualify solely because it is a customer, client, parent, subsidiary,
affiliate, or recipient of consulting services; it must itself employ or have
employed Jihad Khawaja.

The Licensor grants each Qualifying Employer a perpetual, worldwide,
non-exclusive, non-transferable, royalty-free license to use, copy, study,
modify, and internally distribute the Software for its own internal business
and enterprise operations, including commercial operations, without a paid
license, separate agreement, registration, or further approval. This grant
covers organization-wide use by its employees and contractors acting solely
on its behalf, including use in its repositories, CI/CD pipelines, and internal
tools. The Qualifying Employer is responsible for their compliance with this
license. Internal modifications need not be published or disclosed.

This employer permission applies retroactively to the Software distributed
under license version 1.0, as well as under this and later license versions,
including copies already obtained and past use within this section's scope.
For such past use, no license fee is owed, and the Licensor waives claims based
solely on the absence of a paid commercial or enterprise license under earlier
terms. A Qualifying Employer may rely on this grant even when its copy includes
an earlier license without the employer exception. All other conditions and
third-party license requirements remain applicable.

Once an entity qualifies, these rights continue after Jihad Khawaja's employment
ends, regardless of the reason. They apply to all existing versions and
automatically to all future versions of the Software that the Licensor makes
available, even after that employment ends and even if a future version carries
different license terms, to the extent the Licensor owns or controls the rights
needed for this grant. No later change to this license withdraws or narrows
this grant for an entity that has qualified, subject to section 6 and applicable
law. This grant does not require the Licensor to create or deliver future
versions or provide support, maintenance, or access to private repositories.

This exception does not permit resale, external redistribution, sublicensing,
offering the Software's functionality as a hosted service to third parties, or
using it to perform work on behalf of other organizations. Those activities
require a separate paid commercial license. It does permit using the Software
internally to develop and maintain the Qualifying Employer's own commercial
products and services; those products and services may be sold to customers
provided they do not distribute the Software or offer its functionality to
third parties. This exception does not grant rights to third-party materials
beyond their own licenses or transfer ownership of the Software.

